1
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:06,401
Yes, someone suddenly came up
behind me and pointed a gun at me,

2
00:00:06,451 --> 00:00:08,020
I didn't see their face.

3
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:12,060
Apparently it was Kankichi.

4
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:13,240
He's coming right away, apparently.

5
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:14,800
How's he coming?

6
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,080
Aloha!

7
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:20,420
Sorry to keep you waiting!

8
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:21,900
Kankichi!

9
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:25,940
Yoho!

10
00:00:26,640 --> 00:00:27,840
I did it!

11
00:00:28,240 --> 00:00:29,540
Kankichi, you're so cool.

12
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:31,320
Heh, thanks.

13
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:35,560
Despite what you say,
you seem to be having a good time.

14
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:37,020
So, the victim is...

15
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:40,480
That refined-looking
married couple over there.

16
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:44,360
Apparently, a diamond and ruby pendant
worth 100,000 dollars was stolen from them.

17
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:45,560
As for the culprit...

18
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,760
they say it was a pair of men.

19
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:50,300
They were held at gunpoint from behind, so

20
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:51,980
they say they didn't see the faces.

21
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:55,260
I see. Is there any sign the culprit fled?

22
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:57,580
We've been on the deck the whole time.

23
00:00:57,580 --> 00:00:59,420
There was nothing like that.

24
00:01:00,180 --> 00:01:03,680
So that means the culprit is
still somewhere on this ship.

25
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:05,280
I suppose that's the case.

26
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:08,940
Then the culprit is as good as caught.

27
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:15,160
I called the coast guard on my way here,
so they should be arriving any moment.

28
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:17,780
Here they come!

29
00:01:17,780 --> 00:01:19,660
Hey, over here!

30
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:23,080
Oh no, this is bad. What do we do?

31
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:25,820
Relax, they didn't see our faces.

32
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:28,900
As long as we hide the pendant somewhere,
we'll be fine.

33
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:29,740
I see.

34
00:01:32,660 --> 00:01:35,580
Now we just leave the
rest to the coast guard.

35
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:36,340
Kankichi!

36
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:37,080
Yeah?

37
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:38,480
I need to pee.

38
00:01:38,480 --> 00:01:40,180
Can't be helped.

39
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:42,500
Here, it's here.

40
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,300
Kankichi, hold this for me.

41
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:44,780
Yeah.

42
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:52,200
I can't hold it much longer.

43
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:23,400
Ankichi

44
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:25,600
Ankichi

45
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:28,660
Are you done with the lemon yet?

46
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:29,220
Yeah.

47
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:31,860
I dozed off, dammit.

48
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:33,140
Thanks.

49
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:36,440
We have to get back quick.

50
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:37,360
Hurry!

51
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,540
Here we go.

52
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:51,240
Alright, we did it!

53
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:53,740
Good work, Dolphin Decker.

54
00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:05,900
Now, today's second event.

55
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:09,320
We're in the final stretch of the
longboard half-island race around Oan Island.

56
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:12,200
The racers who safely rescued the beauty

57
00:03:12,200 --> 00:03:14,180
are crossing the finish
line one after another.

58
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:16,500
Yes, good work.

59
00:03:16,500 --> 00:03:19,280
Well, you came in last,
so you get zero points.

60
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:19,800
Yeah.

61
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:26,680
Alright, I've moved up to third place!

62
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:29,800
Alright, I'll catch up to
the top before the day is over.

63
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,220
What's the third race?

64
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:35,860
And the final race of the
day is a test of stamina!

65
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:38,420
Animal Piggyback Marathon!

66
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:41,060
Carrying these adorable animals on your back

67
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:43,440
and finish the race all the
way to the Waikiki finish line.

68
00:03:45,480 --> 00:03:48,780
Wow! Incredibly,
Ryocchi is carrying an elephant!

69
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:52,320
Just finishing while carrying
the elephant earns 100 points!

70
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:54,720
And if you cross the finish line in first place,
that's another 100 points!

71
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:57,020
That's a total of 200 points!

72
00:03:57,220 --> 00:03:59,880
Ugh, I'm going to shoot straight to the top!

73
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:01,920
Excuse me, coming through!

74
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:03,460
Hey, get back here, you bastard!

75
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:09,060
You...

76
00:04:13,260 --> 00:04:15,820
Hey, this is no time to be eating that crap!

77
00:04:31,820 --> 00:04:34,720
What, you scattered bait
and set the animals rampaging!

78
00:04:35,180 --> 00:04:36,940
Who would do something like this?

79
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:41,880
You...

80
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:44,280
This bulge isn't just for show!

81
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:46,620
When an incident happens on land,

82
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:49,200
swim trunks alone solve everything.

83
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:52,500
Kaipan Zeka has arrived!

84
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:54,900
You're in the race's way too

85
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:58,180
I'll give this one to the elephant.

86
00:04:58,180 --> 00:04:58,580
What?

87
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:00,340
Heykyū!

88
00:05:05,820 --> 00:05:07,080
It's Zagarel!

89
00:05:13,960 --> 00:05:16,100
Hey, don't eat that junk!

90
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:19,440
It's you again.

91
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:21,100
Hello? What's up?

92
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,600
Did you find the culprit?

93
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,420
In the end, we couldn't find them.

94
00:05:25,420 --> 00:05:27,980
We've only just been let go now.

95
00:05:28,560 --> 00:05:29,800
So, what do you want?

96
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:33,300
I'm thinking of taking a
commemorative photo in Hawaii now.

97
00:05:33,300 --> 00:05:34,540
You come too.

98
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:37,860
What? I don't have to go, do I?

99
00:05:39,060 --> 00:05:41,380
They really want to take a photo with you.

100
00:05:41,840 --> 00:05:43,020
Or is it something else?

101
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:45,220
Or is there some reason
you can't come over here?

102
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:47,200
Hey, it's nothing like that.

103
00:05:47,200 --> 00:05:48,880
Got it, I'm coming right away.

104
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:50,780
Gross.

105
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:51,880
So, anyway.

106
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:54,200
I'm going to take a little
detour off the course.

107
00:05:55,220 --> 00:05:57,120
Wait, I won't let you.

108
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:59,440
If you want to move forward,
you'll have to face me first.

109
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:01,060
Don't you dare go forward!

110
00:06:01,060 --> 00:06:02,820
I'm making a U-turn.

111
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:04,340
No arguments!

112
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:06,680
Now, this is a true showdown!

113
00:06:11,180 --> 00:06:13,220
I don't have time to play around with you.

114
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:14,620
Alright, let's go.

115
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:22,560
I'm going to keep at it nonstop.

116
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:32,400
Kankichi's really taking his time, isn't he?

117
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,580
Doesn't he know where this photo studio is?

118
00:06:37,260 --> 00:06:51,160


119
00:06:51,160 --> 00:06:53,820
How about this one? Amazing, right?

120
00:06:53,820 --> 00:06:55,380
Heh heh, how's that?

121
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:59,100
You're as pale as a sheet. Are you alright?

122
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:00,360
Ugh, I see.

123
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:02,460
Alright, then I'm taking the picture now.

124
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:04,620
Come on, smile. Say cheese!

125
00:07:10,460 --> 00:07:12,080
Don't call me again!

126
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:14,352
What on earth is that guy,

127
00:07:14,402 --> 00:07:19,380
why would he even come to Hawaii?

128
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:26,580
Well, here in Hawaii on Oahu Island,
we're covering

129
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:29,960
the Family Iron Man Baka
Ichidai Showdown in Hawaii.

130
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:33,940
The final race of day two, the animal
piggyback marathon, is nearing its end.

131
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:37,640
Only racer number 30,
Kankichi Ryotsu, is left,

132
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:39,860
but he seems to be running very late.

133
00:07:39,860 --> 00:07:43,000
Does that mean he's in danger?

134
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,480
Can't be helped.

135
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:47,520
What is it?

136
00:07:47,520 --> 00:07:48,440
He's here!

137
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:56,100
This is a great shot!

138
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:59,100
Camera standby!
Come on, keep the commentary going!

139
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:01,220
Ladies and gentlemen, take a look!

140
00:08:01,220 --> 00:08:03,540
Racer number 30, Kankichi Ryotsu,

141
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:06,080
has returned carrying
an elephant on his back!

142
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:10,760
Ryotsu entered this race all alone,
without any request from his family.

143
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:14,580
What an iron-willed fellow he is!

144
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:17,100
Without setting the elephant down,

145
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:21,160
he's getting one step
closer to the finish line.

146
00:08:23,620 --> 00:08:27,620
Ryotsu is receiving applause
and cheers from the crowd.

147
00:08:27,620 --> 00:08:30,760
Now, the elephant reaches the goal.

148
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:39,260
We somehow only got 100
points for the elephant.

149
00:08:44,560 --> 00:08:45,140
We've arrived.

150
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:50,500
Kankichi.

151
00:08:50,500 --> 00:08:53,820
Kankichi, what on earth happened to you?

152
00:08:54,020 --> 00:08:56,900
M-m-m-Matoi.

153
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:01,100
Are you a family member of Ryotsu-san?

154
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:02,980
E-, well, yes.

155
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:08,140
I heard all the family
members were sick in bed.

156
00:09:08,140 --> 00:09:10,740
What are you talking about?

157
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:20,340
Matoi

158
00:09:20,340 --> 00:09:21,680
You're awake?

159
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:22,860
This is...

160
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:25,140
Don't worry, it's a hotel room.

161
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:25,880
I see.

162
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:28,800
Why didn't you tell us, Kankichi?

163
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:30,460
What are you talking about?

164
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:31,680
Don't play dumb.

165
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:35,920
I heard everything from the
producer of Tetsujin Bakkaichidai.

166
00:09:35,920 --> 00:09:38,680
Gikuremon, Gepard, and the others...

167
00:09:39,220 --> 00:09:41,740
They've all gone to see the fire dance show.

168
00:09:42,960 --> 00:09:45,260
So you're the only one talking to me, then.

169
00:09:45,980 --> 00:09:50,700
You're really an idiot, struggling on
your own until you've ended up like this.

170
00:09:50,700 --> 00:09:53,660
Stupidity is something you're born with,
after all.

171
00:09:54,540 --> 00:09:58,500
If you'd just said a word,
I would have joined in too.

172
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:03,400
No, I owe you and your family a lot.

173
00:10:03,860 --> 00:10:07,400
I simply wanted you to
enjoy the Hawaii trip.

174
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:10,380
You're saying something
totally out of character.

175
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:15,800
I've got a bit more respect for you.
I'll join tomorrow's race too.

176
00:10:16,340 --> 00:10:23,680
Well, it's out now, so there's no helping it.
Truth is, I figured I'd reached my limit doing it alone. Sorry, I'm counting on you.

177
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:26,560
Haah!

178
00:10:29,900 --> 00:10:31,080
Aaaaaah!

179
00:10:38,100 --> 00:10:42,020
Aaaaaah!

180
00:10:42,020 --> 00:10:44,740
If we look for the Maga-musume,
we'll somehow make the problem work, nya.

181
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:48,740
Granny

182
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:51,460
Help me!

183
00:10:51,900 --> 00:10:52,580
Wait!

184
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:58,180
If he's that energetic,
he should be fine, right?

185
00:10:58,180 --> 00:11:01,000
Is something wrong with Kankichi?

186
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:09,340
That's why, if Granny finds out about the race,
it'll be a disaster.

187
00:11:09,340 --> 00:11:13,520
I see, so that was it.
Sorry for doubting you.

188
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:16,600
I don't mind at all.

189
00:11:16,600 --> 00:11:20,200
But Lemon really does like Kankichi,
doesn't he?

190
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:23,420
Because everyone only looks
at Kankichi's bad points.

191
00:11:23,420 --> 00:11:26,200
They just don't see the
real good in Kankichi.

192
00:11:26,740 --> 00:11:28,700
Yeah, that's true.

193
00:11:28,700 --> 00:11:31,720
But keep this a secret from everyone, okay?

194
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:32,540
Got it.

195
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:37,580
Today is a city sightseeing tour.

196
00:11:39,380 --> 00:11:41,060
Matoi, you're not going either?

197
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:43,860
Yeah, I've got a bit of a cold, you know.

198
00:11:43,860 --> 00:11:47,740
Kankichi, if you try anything funny with Matoi,
you'll pay for it.

199
00:11:47,740 --> 00:11:49,300
I told you, it's a misunderstanding.

200
00:11:49,880 --> 00:11:53,000
Don't worry, Matoi's stronger than Kankichi.

201
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,540
If anything happens,
I'll knock him flying, so it's fine.

202
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,120
Yeah, that's true.

203
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:05,700
Hey, let me on that one too!

204
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:08,440
Well, I'm off then.

205
00:12:09,340 --> 00:12:11,440
Have fun! Grandma too, see you!

206
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:22,780
We're going too Leave it to us!

207
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:38,240
Well, it's finally the last day.

208
00:12:38,240 --> 00:12:40,780
It has unfolded here on the island of Oahu.

209
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:42,980
Iron Man Baka Ichidai in Hawaii

210
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:47,420
Today's events are all the same
race on the same course as day one,

211
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:50,120
but everyone will be competing in pairs.

212
00:12:50,680 --> 00:12:53,680
And I was going to let
Kankichi rest for once.

213
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,240
Two people per team?

214
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:58,560
Don't worry, I'm good on a bicycle.

215
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:04,760
The pedals are heavy.

216
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,080
Ow!

217
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:10,640
Th-this is bad! Forward, just once!

218
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:14,960
It's the final day!
A harsher ordeal has been prepared!

219
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:15,960
Damn it!

220
00:13:27,460 --> 00:13:30,680
Kankichi! Are you alright going so fast?

221
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:34,100
If it comes to this, I'm ready to collapse!

222
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:46,640
Now, everyone,
here is the statue of King Kamehameha!

223
00:14:05,580 --> 00:14:06,680
What do you think you're doing?

224
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:12,280
Let go of my belly!

225
00:14:12,280 --> 00:14:13,260
Nice going!

226
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:14,540
Hey, what are you doing?

227
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:16,280
If it comes to this, the brat goes down too!

228
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:24,000
This is bad. Things have gotten serious.

229
00:14:29,040 --> 00:14:30,800
Wow, Kankichi, that's amazing!

230
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,480
He's way out in front in first place!

231
00:14:33,700 --> 00:14:36,500
We crossed the finish line and
got 100 points for the first race!

232
00:14:37,060 --> 00:14:39,700
First across the line
is the Ryotsu Joy Team!

233
00:14:40,480 --> 00:14:42,600
With this, Ryotsu's team gets 100 points!

234
00:14:42,600 --> 00:14:45,340
And they've jumped into first place overall!

235
00:14:46,020 --> 00:14:46,380
Right.

236
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:48,840
Next is the 10-kilometer entertainment race

237
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:49,640
Let's go.

238
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:50,340
Yeah.

239
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:52,340
Hey, wait up!

240
00:14:53,340 --> 00:14:54,060
What is it?

241
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:58,260
Today's event requires
you to swim wearing this.

242
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:00,760
What?

243
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:03,040
What? Did you lay a hand on Tesukabuto?

244
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:07,900
I told you the final day
had brutal trials prepared!

245
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,920
Hey, Matoi! Hurry up!

246
00:15:11,780 --> 00:15:13,860
If I put this on, I can't swim!

247
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:16,100
Huh?

248
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:22,300
W-what, again? Hello?

249
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:26,320
Kankichi, it's bad! Lemon's been kidnapped!

250
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:28,720
W-what?

251
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:34,640
We're safe now that we've come this far.

252
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:35,960
Now then, little girl.

253
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:38,220
Hand over the stuffed toy.

254
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:39,380
No way!

255
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:42,080
How about this?

256
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:45,660
Lemon!

257
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:46,360
What?

258
00:15:49,480 --> 00:15:51,340
Lemon!

259
00:15:51,340 --> 00:15:53,300
Hatch! Matoi!

260
00:15:53,300 --> 00:15:55,320
Speed it up!

261
00:15:59,040 --> 00:16:01,460
You can't, not while you're
wearing something that heavy.

262
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,200
I don't have time to take it off now.

263
00:16:03,620 --> 00:16:04,000
Come on.

264
00:16:09,020 --> 00:16:09,660
What?

265
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:12,300
Damn it, at least Tagma...

266
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:33,880
Matoi, are you okay?

267
00:16:36,180 --> 00:16:37,320
Somehow, yeah.

268
00:16:38,540 --> 00:16:40,320
Whatever you do, don't let go!

269
00:16:41,260 --> 00:16:42,180
Got it.

270
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:54,720
It's the Special
Investigations Division guys.

271
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:57,740
Isn't that Ryotsu?

272
00:16:58,320 --> 00:16:59,700
You showed up at just the right time.

273
00:16:59,700 --> 00:17:02,380
Sorry, but we don't have
time to deal with you.

274
00:17:03,900 --> 00:17:06,540
We got so caught up playing,
we lost track of time.

275
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:08,980
We completely forgot we had a mission.

276
00:17:08,980 --> 00:17:11,280
Well then, farewell.

277
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:13,080
Hey, at least help me out!

278
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:15,680
You can see what kind of
situation this is, right?

279
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:16,960
Heartless jerks!

280
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:20,460
Matoi!

281
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:23,580
Climb up from there along the bicycle.

282
00:17:24,260 --> 00:17:25,020
Hurry!

283
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:26,300
Got it!

284
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:34,700
Just climb up using my
head as a stepping stone.

285
00:17:34,700 --> 00:17:36,240
But that's...

286
00:17:36,240 --> 00:17:37,220
Just do it.

287
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:38,400
Sorry about this.

288
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:43,060
Kankichi.

289
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:49,200
Why a bicycle of all things?

290
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:51,900
Without this, there are too many of them.

291
00:17:51,900 --> 00:17:53,040
Kankichi.

292
00:17:53,040 --> 00:17:53,720
Get on.

293
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:54,220
Yeah.

294
00:17:57,140 --> 00:18:00,640
Now then, little miss,
nobody's coming to save you anymore.

295
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:03,160
Let's have that stuffed toy over here.

296
00:18:03,620 --> 00:18:05,260
No way, I won't hand it over!

297
00:18:05,260 --> 00:18:06,320
What's wrong?

298
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:10,540
Hurry up, we've been waiting.

299
00:18:10,540 --> 00:18:13,240
Him again?
He should've fallen off the cliff.

300
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:15,420
Don't think you can get away from me.

301
00:18:24,300 --> 00:18:26,520
In this narrow tunnel, we can't escape!

302
00:18:31,840 --> 00:18:33,940
Uh-oh, hold on tight!

303
00:18:37,260 --> 00:18:37,620
What?

304
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:38,280
Daikichi!

305
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:40,880
Lemon, I'm saving you now!

306
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:42,380
Stop it!

307
00:18:46,340 --> 00:18:48,100
We've got the pistol, we're in control!

308
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:49,740
The tunnel...

309
00:18:56,900 --> 00:18:57,940
Stop the car!

310
00:18:57,940 --> 00:18:58,780
Shut up!

311
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:00,260
I said stop!

312
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:20,020
Even you villains, give up!

313
00:19:24,740 --> 00:19:26,900
You were on the cruiser yesterday.

314
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:30,960
What? So you're the jewel thieves?

315
00:19:31,760 --> 00:19:36,440
That's right. We hid the pendant
inside this brat's stuffed toy.

316
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:40,040
What? Then that's why you took Lemon...

317
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:43,900
Damn you! Dragging a kid into this!

318
00:19:47,080 --> 00:19:51,180
I'll never forgive you bastards!

319
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:56,120
Kankichi!

320
00:20:00,540 --> 00:20:01,380
Kankichi!

321
00:20:01,380 --> 00:20:03,320
You idiot!

322
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:06,180
There was another gun after all.

323
00:20:06,800 --> 00:20:08,080
Kankichi.

324
00:20:09,140 --> 00:20:10,000
Hey, brat!

325
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,300
Lemon.

326
00:20:11,760 --> 00:20:13,000
Hand over the stuffed toy.

327
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:13,980
No way!

328
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:17,880
This stuffed toy went to Kyoto for training,
I told her.

329
00:20:17,880 --> 00:20:22,240
It's a treasure she bought for
Lemon with her very first paycheck.

330
00:20:22,240 --> 00:20:25,300
You're going to hand
over Lemon's stuffed toy?

331
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:27,720
No! Absolutely not!

332
00:20:28,260 --> 00:20:31,080
Damn it,
we'll just have to take it by force!

333
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:33,760
Stop!

334
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:40,780
Kankichi!

335
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:44,360
Thank goodness I was wearing this armor!

336
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:46,060
Lemon! Run!

337
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:47,400
Kankichi!

338
00:20:49,680 --> 00:20:51,360
Matoi! Leave Lemon to you!

339
00:20:52,200 --> 00:20:53,520
Damn it!

340
00:20:56,120 --> 00:21:07,640
!

341
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:09,920
You always do things Lemon hates,
you bastard!

342
00:21:10,460 --> 00:21:12,320
You bastard, you bastard!

343
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:14,320
There, how about this!

344
00:21:14,520 --> 00:21:15,160
Chaaa!

345
00:21:15,380 --> 00:21:18,960
Well, I'll let you off the hook for today!

346
00:21:27,560 --> 00:21:29,720
I knew you'd come and save me.

347
00:21:30,320 --> 00:21:31,860
Haha, I see.

348
00:21:35,480 --> 00:21:37,480
Alright, let's leave the culprits to them.

349
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:39,920
Matoi, we're getting back into the race!

350
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:43,620
We can still make it to the final event.

351
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:46,700
Finished.

352
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:50,220
The winners are Mr. Suzuki's team.

353
00:21:50,700 --> 00:21:52,000
Congratulations.

354
00:21:52,620 --> 00:21:53,320
Damn it!

355
00:21:53,940 --> 00:21:55,660
The danger to my balance took its toll.

356
00:21:57,900 --> 00:21:59,100
That was a little close, wasn't it?

357
00:22:00,180 --> 00:22:03,200
Well, it couldn't be helped.
There were accidents, too.

358
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:03,720
Kankichi.

359
00:22:03,720 --> 00:22:06,940
You two must be exhausted.

360
00:22:06,940 --> 00:22:10,100
We've heard the whole story, everyone.

361
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:12,500
Thank you so much for saving Lemon.

362
00:22:12,940 --> 00:22:15,100
Still, you're a sneaky one, aren't you?

363
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:17,840
Keeping the race a secret like that.

364
00:22:18,320 --> 00:22:21,480
No, I just wanted to thank everyone
who's been looking after me all this time.

365
00:22:21,480 --> 00:22:25,000
by letting you all enjoy a trip to Hawaii.

366
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,820
Thank you for your hard work.

367
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:33,560
Too bad, Producer. If not for that danger along the way,
we'd have won for sure.

368
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:35,660
We missed out on 100 million yen.

369
00:22:36,160 --> 00:22:39,600
A hundred million yen?
What do you mean, a hundred million yen?

370
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:43,820
It's the prize for this race.
If you win, it's 100 million yen.

371
00:22:43,820 --> 00:22:47,520
Kankichi, you didn't say a word about that!

372
00:22:48,260 --> 00:22:52,760
You were saying all those cool things,
but that was the real goal all along?

373
00:22:52,760 --> 00:22:54,740
No, no, no, it's not like that!

374
00:22:54,740 --> 00:22:58,620
Everyone, there are luxury
prizes for the top three, right?

375
00:22:58,620 --> 00:23:02,540
Yes, exactly.
A round-the-world trip for the whole family.

376
00:23:02,540 --> 00:23:03,680
Round-the-world trip.

377
00:23:03,680 --> 00:23:07,560
Did you hear? That's amazing!
Everyone, a trip around the world!

378
00:23:07,560 --> 00:23:08,760
Did you do it, Kankichi?

379
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:09,980
Look at the size of it!

380
00:23:11,980 --> 00:23:14,560
See, when it counts,
I can really deliver, right?

381
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:18,480
But this is a free invitation
to the next project,

382
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:21,180
for all of you,
a race held while going around the world

383
00:23:21,180 --> 00:23:25,340
Family Ironman Idiot One-Car Race,
and you'll be taking part in it.

384
00:23:25,340 --> 00:23:28,120
What, are we doing this race again?

385
00:23:28,120 --> 00:23:30,460
While going around the world?

386
00:23:30,460 --> 00:23:33,060
Our bodies can't take that, you idiot!

387
00:23:33,060 --> 00:23:38,280
Kankichi, you don't seriously
expect us to do that race, do you?

388
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:40,220
No, no, no way.

389
00:23:41,320 --> 00:23:43,360
Starting the new year
off with such bad luck.

390
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:48,260
Aaaah, I hate those Ironman races too!

391
00:23:57,780 --> 00:24:07,360
Excuse me...
yes why is it, why is it, why, why is it?

392
00:24:07,360 --> 00:24:10,140
From today, I'm the Tetsuwan
friend who sings the ending.

393
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:13,460
So...

394
00:24:38,620 --> 00:24:42,980
Even in sandals, he can run incredibly fast,

395
00:24:42,980 --> 00:24:44,000
I wonder why.

396
00:24:46,240 --> 00:24:50,840
Ryo-san always has his sleeves rolled up,

397
00:24:50,840 --> 00:24:51,900
I wonder why.

398
00:24:53,200 --> 00:24:57,160
he's a total mess, yet everyone adores him,

399
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:58,300
I wonder why.

400
00:24:58,840 --> 00:25:00,380
I wonder why.

401
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:04,200
It's not that it really matters,

402
00:25:05,220 --> 00:25:10,900
but why is this anime's title so long?

403
00:25:13,360 --> 00:25:15,540
I wonder why.

404
00:25:15,540 --> 00:25:17,920
I wonder why.

405
00:25:20,980 --> 00:25:22,260
I wonder why

406
00:25:22,260 --> 00:25:23,660
I wonder why

407
00:25:23,660 --> 00:25:24,380
I wonder why

408
00:25:24,380 --> 00:25:26,600
I wonder why

409
00:25:26,600 --> 00:25:27,900
I wonder why

410
00:25:27,900 --> 00:25:29,320
I wonder why

411
00:25:29,320 --> 00:25:29,500
Why is it

412
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:29,880
Why is it

413
00:25:29,880 --> 00:25:30,620
Why is it

414
00:25:30,620 --> 00:25:31,540
I wonder why

415
00:25:35,040 --> 00:25:37,180
Thank you for watching

